In my few knightly excursions, I've found it very hard to avoid the "You
caitiff!" penalty, and I'm starting to get frustrated with it.

For instance, I'll come across a monster, take a look at it with ';', and
then hit it, only to find out it was asleep.  Why doesn't the look command
tell you that sort of thing?

Also, I've noticed that the game frequently thinks a monster is fleeing,
even when it looks to me like it is actively trying to chew my head off.
The other night, I was in Sokoban, got to the zoo, and started whacking
away.  A monster started to flee.  I stepped back.  The monster pursued me.
I stepped back again.  He still followed.  I hit '.'.  He hit me.  I decided
that, if he's going to attack me, I can defend myself.  Nope; I'm a caitiff.
WTF??!  Again, looking at the monster with ';' doesn't tell you if it's
fleeing or not.

How can knights know when it's safe to attack?



